From 584f53cce0066f4322ee181535a027f4e209bbbc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Fluorite Integration Role
Date: Sun, 8 Mar 2026 23:05:00 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] grpc-proxy: send agl_shell ready after binding

Upstream-Status: Pending

The gRPC proxy binds successfully to `agl_shell` and `agl_shell_ext`, but it
never transitions the compositor shell client into the ready state. Normal
desktop surfaces stay on the pending list until some shell client issues the
`ready` request.

Background/panel flows work because the original shell-aware client sends
`ready()`. The fluorite NORMAL path does not, so pending surfaces remain with
role NONE and are removed before activation completes.

Issue `agl_shell_ready()` immediately after a successful bind so the compositor
can process pending surfaces for normal applications as well.
---
 grpc-proxy/main-grpc.cpp | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/grpc-proxy/main-grpc.cpp b/grpc-proxy/main-grpc.cpp
index 8964946..b9c7225 100644
--- a/grpc-proxy/main-grpc.cpp
+++ b/grpc-proxy/main-grpc.cpp
@@ -378,6 +378,13 @@ register_shell_ext(void)
 		goto err;
 	}
 
+	LOG("sending agl_shell ready request\n");
+	agl_shell_ready(sh->shell);
+	if (wl_display_roundtrip(sh->wl_display) < 0) {
+		LOG("Failed while waiting for agl_shell ready roundtrip\n");
+		goto err;
+	}
+
 	LOG("agl_shell/agl_shell_ext interfaces OK\n");
 	return sh;
 err:
